;; spec:   §7 (types §2.10, §8.6)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 12
;; audit:  clean
;; swap! is compare-and-retry: when the atom changes while f runs, f
;; runs again on the new content. Here f, on its first run only, has
;; another thread add 10 to the atom and waits for it; the compare then
;; fails (11, not 1), f runs again on 11 and 12 is stored. An
;; interpreter that stored f's first result without the compare lost
;; the other thread's update and returned 2 (adversary finding 001).
;; A swap! whose f changes the atom on every run never finishes, as in
;; Clojure; ownership.md §7 and types §8.6 say so.
(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((a (atom 1))
        (once (atom false)))
    (swap! a (fn (x)
               (do (if @once
                       ()
                       (do (reset! once true)
                           (join (spawn (fn () (swap! a (fn (y) (+ y 10))))))
                           ()))
                   (+ x 1))))))
